This package installs the current prebuilt DAPHNE userspace runtime into the
PetaLinux image.

Installed payload:
- `/usr/bin/daphneServer`
- `/usr/bin/hermes_udp_srv`
- private runtime libraries under `/usr/lib/daphne-server`
- `BUILD-METADATA.txt` describing the staged source bundle

Provenance status:
- the checked-in payload is a legacy external binary import
- its digest is verified, but it is not reproducible from this repository
- it does not implement the dual-gateware command-line contract and the recipe
  deliberately rejects it at `do_fetch`
- production release therefore requires a separately qualified runtime bundle
- `scripts/petalinux/stage_runtime_into_project.sh` is the only staging entry
  point

Qualification contract:
- keep `BUILD-METADATA.txt` and, when supplied, `SHA256SUMS` beside the input
  tarball; the stager preserves the rich metadata instead of replacing it
- metadata must bind the exact tarball and bundled `daphneServer`, identify the
  server commit pinned by `daphne-server-contract.inc`, and record a clean
  AArch64 build with passing QEMU validation
- the executable must expose both `--gateware-mode` and
  `--expected-gateware-build-id`
- a bare tarball can still be staged for inspection, but its generated
  `daphne-server-version.inc` remains unqualified and cannot build the release

Design intent:
- keep the package layout independent of `/home/petalinux`
- preserve deterministic runtime libraries via a private libdir
- let the service layer start `daphneServer` and Hermes from normal system
  paths
